  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nCooler and drier air works into the region through today behind\na cold front that crossed last night. Highs will range from the\nupper 60s north to near 80 degrees near the coast. Winds will be\nsteady out of the WNW while some onshore winds will likely\ndevelop this afternoon near the coast. Broad high pressure over\nthe Great Lakes slowly slides east through the weekend bringing\nfair weather. Day time highs will generally be in the 80s with\nonshore winds keeping coastal areas cooler than the interior.\nFavorable radiational cooling conditions will bring lows into\nthe 40s and 50s tonight and again Friday night.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\n\nEnsembles are in good agreement that troughing will deepen over\nthe Northeast Monday through the middle of next. This will allow\nfor daily chances for showers while pinning down systems moving\nthrough the trough is difficult at this time. The NBM generally\nkeeps PoPs below 30 percent Monday and increases PoPs to around\n50 percent Tuesday and Wednesday.",
